.TH KMPLIFY-NODE 1 "2026-09-05" "kmplify-node 0.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kmplify-node \- lend a machine's GPU, CPU and local models to a KMPLIFY
compute fabric
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kmplify-node
.RI [ run ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kmplify-node
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kmplify-node
is the provider agent for the KMPLIFY Compute Fabric. It joins a fabric over
one outbound connection, advertises the machine's hardware and the models its
local inference engine serves, and delivers the jobs the fabric sends. Nothing
listens on the network unless the LAN router is switched on.
.PP
The same binary carries a terminal dashboard
.RB ( tui ),
a desktop window
.RB ( gui )
and the LAN router, which turns the kmplify-nodes on one local network into a
personal inference cluster.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR run " [" \-\-router ]
Join the fabric and serve, logging to standard output. This is the default
when no command is given. With
.B \-\-router
also run the LAN router in this process.
.TP
.BR tui " [" \-\-router "] [" \-\-attach "|" \-\-standalone ]
Live dashboard. Attaches to the node already running here and drives it, or
starts one when none runs.
.TP
.BR gui " [" \-\-attach "|" \-\-standalone ]
Desktop window: this node, the LAN router and the other nodes on this network.
Attaches like
.B tui
does.
.TP
.BR check " [" \-\-json "] [" \-\-timeout " \fISECS\fR]"
Preflight this host (engines, GPU, Docker), then exit.
.TP
.BR status " [" \-\-json ]
One-shot report of the running node.
.TP
.B id
Print this install's node id.
.TP
.BI set " KEY=VALUE" \|...
Change what this machine lends, durably and without a restart.
.B "set \-\-list"
shows the keys,
.B "set \-\-clear"
.I KEY
returns one to the environment's value.
.TP
.B init
First-run wizard: engine, sharing, preflight.
.TP
.B engines
Scan localhost for inference engines.
.TP
.BR peers " [" \fIVERB\fR " \|...]"
Who may use this machine: list, approve, block, invite.
.TP
.B rewards
Delivered work, and an optional payout companion.
.TP
.BR version ", " help
Version with build stamp; this text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output for
.BR check ", " status " and " peers .
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECS"
Per-probe ceiling in
.B check
(default 5).
.TP
.B \-\-attach
For
.BR tui " and " gui :
require a running node, never start one.
.TP
.B \-\-standalone
For
.BR tui " and " gui :
run the node (and the router) in this process.
.TP
.B \-\-router
For
.BR run " and " tui :
also run the LAN router.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the built-in help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version and build stamp.
.PP
Every configuration flag below sets the environment variable beside it; a
flag overrides what a unit file sets:
.BR \-\-gateway ", " \-\-ollama ", " \-\-colibri ", " \-\-node\-dir ", "
.BR \-\-country ", " \-\-workloads ", " \-\-max\-cpus ", " \-\-max\-vram\-mb ", "
.BR \-\-max\-ram\-mb ", " \-\-max\-disk\-gb ", " \-\-approval\-mode ", "
.BR \-\-gpu\-backend ", " \-\-[no\-]share\-inference ", " \-\-[no\-]share\-cpu ", "
.BR \-\-[no\-]functions ", " \-\-[no\-]share\-vectors .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PROVIDER_GATEWAY_URL
URL of the fabric to join.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_BASE
Local model server (Ollama, vLLM, LiteLLM, TGI). Default localhost.
.TP
.B COLIBRI_BASE
Optional colibri gateway for frontier models.
.TP
.B KMPLIFY_NODE_DIR
Identity, settings, status and control directory. Default
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kmplify-node ,
falling back to
.IR ~/.config/kmplify-node .
.TP
.B PROVIDER_COUNTRY
ISO alpha-2 country declared to the fabric; empty means undeclared.
.TP
.B PROVIDER_WORKLOADS
Template ids to host as container sessions.
.TP
.BR PROVIDER_MAX_CPUS ", " PROVIDER_MAX_VRAM_MB ", " PROVIDER_MAX_RAM_MB ", " PROVIDER_MAX_DISK_GB
Ceilings on what sessions may use and on what is advertised.
.TP
.B PROVIDER_APPROVAL_MODE
.BR auto " or " manual
consumer admission.
.TP
.BR PROVIDER_SHARE_INFERENCE ", " PROVIDER_SHARE_CPU ", " PROVIDER_FUNCTIONS ", " PROVIDER_SHARE_VECTORS
Switches for serving inference jobs (default on), lending CPU threads and RAM,
hosting signed Wasm functions and hosting vector collections (default off).
.TP
.B KMPLIFY_GPU_BACKEND
Force the accelerator:
.BR cuda ", " rocm ", " oneapi ", " metal " or " cpu .
.TP
.B KMPLIFY_ROUTER_PORTS
The router's ports as
.IR info,ollama,openai
(default 14418,11440,11441).
.TP
.B KMPLIFY_NODE_NAME
The name the router announces (default: the hostname).
.PP
A malformed value is a startup error, never a silent fallback.
.SH THE LAN ROUTER
Opt-in per machine and off by default, because it is the one part of the
program that listens on the network. It announces one
.B _kmplify-node._tcp
record on the local link and binds three ports:
.B 14418
(node-info, pairing, engine control),
.B 11440
(Ollama-compatible routing proxy) and
.B 11441
(OpenAI-compatible routing proxy). Pairing is a six-digit PIN authenticating
a SPAKE2 exchange; paired nodes talk over mutual TLS pinned to each other's
certificate fingerprints. Requests from this machine are routed anywhere in
the cluster; paired nodes are served by this node's own engine; anything
else is refused.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/kmplify-node.service
Unit for a headless node, installed but not enabled. It runs as the
.B kmplify
user with
.I /var/lib/kmplify-node
as the node directory; see
.IR /usr/share/doc/kmplify-node/docs/HEADLESS-NODE.md .
.TP
.I /etc/kmplify-node.env
Environment for the unit; a template is at
.IR /usr/share/doc/kmplify-node/kmplify-node.env.example .
.TP
.IR "<node dir>/status.json" ", " "<node dir>/control/"
What the running node publishes and where a dashboard leaves its orders.
.TP
.IR "<node dir>/router.json" ", " "<node dir>/control/router/" ", " "<node dir>/router/"
The router's published state, its orders, and its certificate and cluster.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR /usr/share/doc/kmplify-node/README.md ,
.IR /usr/share/doc/kmplify-node/docs/ROUTER.md ,
.UR https://github.com/kmplify/kmplify-node
the repository
.UE .
